-- title:
--   Separability of level-M Laurent field over L(j)
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field equipped with a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structure, and let $N$, $M$ be nonzero natural numbers. Write $j_q \in \mathbb{Q}((q))$ for `jq`, the Laurent series $q^{-1}$ times the image in $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ of the integral power series `jNum`, and let `modularFunctionFieldFull N` be the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the divisor expansions $\{\,$`qExpand ℚ d jq`$: d \mid N,\ d \neq 0\,\}$. Applying the coefficientwise ring homomorphism `coeffEmb L` induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ and adjoining the image over $L$ inside $L((q))$ produces the intermediate fields `laurentBaseChange L (modularFunctionFieldFull N)` and `laurentBaseChange L (modularFunctionFieldFull M)`; assume the former is contained in the latter, with inclusion `hle`. Let $E$ denote `IntermediateField.extendScalars hle`, that is the level-$M$ field regarded as an intermediate field over the level-$N$ field. The assertion is that $E$ is a separable algebra over the intermediate field obtained by adjoining to $L$, inside $E$, the single element given by the image of $j_q$ under `coeffEmb L`.
--
--   This is the separability hypothesis required by the weight-two $q$-expansion computation of the trace of a pulled-back differential at the $j$-generator: it says that the level-$M$ Laurent function field is separable over the subfield $L(j)$ generated by the $j$-expansion. It is stated for an arbitrary pair of levels $N \mid M$ in the sense of the inclusion `hle`, and is used by [`ModularCurve.qExpansionDiff_traceDiff_pullbackDiff_smul_D`](thm.html#ModularCurve.qExpansionDiff_traceDiff_pullbackDiff_smul_D); the proof invokes the existence of modular polynomial data, [`ModularCurve.nonempty_modularPolynomialData`](thm.html#ModularCurve.nonempty_modularPolynomialData).
